      "description": "SmallBoatWatch is an independent app published by Reform UK. It is not a government app. It does not represent, and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or acting on behalf of the UK Government, the Home Office or any other government entity.\n\nSmallBoatWatch gives you the daily numbers on small boat crossings of the English Channel, in one place.\n\nABOUT THE DATA Crossing figures are official Home Office statistics, taken from these GOV.UK publications: https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/migrants-detected-crossing-the-english-channel-in-small-boats https://www.gov.uk/government/statistical-data-sets/migrants-detected-crossing-the-english-channel-in-small-boats Cost figures are estimates calculated by Reform UK. They are not official statistics and are not endorsed by the Home Office.\n\nTODAY AT A GLANCE The running total of crossings recorded since 2018, the figure for the latest day in the data, and an estimated cost for the week.\n\nDAY BY DAY Every day since 2018, in one list. See how the latest day compares with the days and weeks before it.\n\nWHOSE WATCH The record of each Prime Minister: crossings during their time in office, the daily average, and the estimated cost.\n\nDAILY ALERT Opt in to one notification a day with the latest figure. Nothing else, no noise. Turn it off any time in Settings.\n\nSHARE THE FIGURE Send the day's number to anyone, as a graphic built for sharing.\n\nSign in with your email address and a one-time code — no password to remember. You can delete your account and its data from inside the app at any time.\n\nEvery figure in the app links back to its GOV.UK source under Settings, so you can check it yourself.\n\nSmallBoatWatch is available in the United Kingdom only.",
